Z||000000||KRMFiero||12-10-2000||01:52 PM||||My dad's boss has a 2000 Grand Prix GTP (and my dad has it on the weekends) and I just noticed it has a pretty good CD-Player but it also has controls on the steering wheel (I kind of like the looks of the steering wheel to)    well anyways would the steering wheel from a new Gran Prix fit in the Fiero?<P><BR>has anyone done this? is it hard?    I might take a trip to our local junk yard and see if i can pull a steering wheel and CD-Player...  I think it would look really nice plus it is kindof like a safty upgrade or something (you dont have to take your hands off the wheel<P>well i'm out<BR>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE<BR>Front - AudioBahn 4 x 10<BR>Headrest - AudioBahn 3 1/2<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||12-10-2000||05:35 PM||||Be very very careful. The airbag may go off. As for if the steering wheel will fit I doubt it due to the mounting of an airbag style steering wheel is different. Some earlier models (without airbags) had the buttons on the steering wheel too. Finally if you do find one you need the VIN # of the car you took it from. The reason is a lot of those style radios were anti-theft. They required a code punched in to turn them on if the power has/was disconnected for a long time. The dealer can look up the required code.||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||12-10-2000||06:06 PM||||thank you, I was woundering about the airbag thing, that sticks.... i never even knew about the code on the radio though, thank you, i have learned something today<BR>hehe<P>bye<BR>Kyle<P><P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE<BR>Front - AudioBahn 4 x 10<BR>Headrest - AudioBahn 3 1/2<P> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||12-11-2000||12:28 AM||||the GM Delco radios have a feature called "Theftlock" -- If you buy one from a yard and find that it is locked, there is a way to get the backup code which is needed to get the unlock code - the VIN of the vehicle the radio came from is not needed (most of the radios from the pick-n-pull won't have the VIN on them anyway -- if you get one and need help unlocking it, call me at the shop (510-233-4376), I can help unlock it for you.......||||reg||1
